{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/292267-the-elder-scrolls-appreciation-discussion-thread","id":292267,"title":"The Elder Scrolls Appreciation/Discussion Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-25T11:42:37-07:00","id":292267,"title":"The Elder Scrolls Appreciation/Discussion Thread","content":"As somebody may have noticed, I'm a huge the Elder Scrolls series buff, to put it mildly. I played Morrowind on its release date, read most of most obscure lore pieces that are not in games, but I enjoy as much the gameplay.<br /> <br /> Basically, if you want to talk about the lore or discuss the gameplay, feel free to post.<br /> <br /> For starters, I'm curious what builds are your favorite. For me it's Archery / Light Armor / Twohanded combiined with healthy dose of stealth. And in the context of Skyrim it pays off for me to go Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T14:44:54-07:00","id":292405,"title":"","content":"I'm always a sneaker on my first play-through. I favored Short Blade in <i>Morrowind</i>, which is probably my favorite of the series.<br /> <br /> I also worked on the series for a year. Got to write some Argonian lore and some stuff about Hircine, though I'm not sure if any of it's in-game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T15:02:27-07:00","id":292447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also worked on the series for a year. Got to write some Argonian lore and some stuff about Hircine, though I'm not sure if any of it's in-game. </div> </div> </div>Hircine is my favorite Daedra along with Sheogorath, so more material is always welcome, and certainly I would appreciate more about Hist, since they are even older than Mer.<br /> <br /> For some reason I never dabbled with Short Weapons. I always preferred to pick off people with bows when stealthy.<br /> <br /> And you mean Elder Scrolls Online? I'm personally not interested in any online RPGs, so I did not form any opinion on it. I more look forward to the sixth part and I have my own speculations.<br /> <br /> I would love if it was set in Hammerfell and PC was either avatar of Make Way God or came into possession of his manifestation as weapon (or both, deal with Cyrus was complicated). Or we could play a nerfed Sword Singer so we get closer look on the other Tonal reality warping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 10-25-2014, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T15:26:24-07:00","id":292459,"title":"","content":"I know is topic as hell but I'm through and trough a Breton Mage/Necromancer. Love Conjuration and Enchatment, but also any of the other &quot;craft&quot; skills as Alchemy. My second favourite race are the Orsimer because of their crafts (Orc Armour is just beatiful). In general I like to make things be it potions or encahnted weapons and armor, though blowing things up with Destruction is also lots of fun.<br /> <br /> One race that intrigues me and that I like a lot, but curiously almost never played, are the Argonians. They have a very, very obscure lore behind their source and the misterious Hist. Same goes for the Bosmer and Khajit.<br /> <br /> Hate the Thalmor with the rage of a thousand suns. How delightful to kill them, raise them and kill them again. Pity it can only be done once.<br /> <br /> Also hate the look of Cirodil (and the Imperials) in Ovblivion. Glad they went back to their roman look in Skyrim.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T15:30:37-07:00","id":292461,"title":"","content":"Who does not hate Thalmor? Even Alduin is more 'sympathetic' because even if he destroys the world new kalpa will happen (though he gone gonzo and it''s implied he wants to rule over the world). Thalmor wants to stop the cycle. But still, Molag Bal is worse, though there is style to his monstrosity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T20:40:08-07:00","id":292633,"title":"","content":"Whenever I play an Elder Scrolls game, I like to make multiple characters and use alternate start mods to have them all follow different stories and quests - it's always a whole tonne of fun to me.<br /> With my current heavily modded play through of Skyrim, I'm playing an Imperial Mage as the Dragonborn, an Argonian Thief, a Dunmer Vampire Assassin and a Wood Elf Warrior.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/292267-the-elder-scrolls-appreciation-discussion-thread?p=292459#post292459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also hate the look of Cirodil (and the Imperials) in Ovblivion. Glad they went back to their roman look in Skyrim.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am still annoyed that Oblivion used 'generic eurofantasy forest', rather than the awesomeness of pseudo-chinese tropical Rome. I cannot believe there's not a mod like that for it yet, considering that a tropical Skyrim mod exists.<br /> I mean, Oblivion was my first game in the series and I did indeed enjoy it, but I just can't look at it the same way after reading what Cyrodiil could have been.<br /> <br /> Heh, as for the Thalmor - I actually kind of like them. Well, not exactly-... I find them interesting bad guys for the most part, and they're pretty fun to kill repeatedly.<br /> Not to mention I love the more-... Horrifying aspects of Altmeri culture. Aspects that the Thalmor more or less embody.<br /> I guess it's more like I love to hate them, then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 10-25-2014, 11:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T04:26:43-07:00","id":292853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am still annoyed that Oblivion used 'generic eurofantasy forest', rather than the awesomeness of pseudo-chinese tropical Rome. I cannot believe there's not a mod like that for it yet, considering that a tropical Skyrim mod exists. </div> </div> </div>A legit explanation is that Talos did it through CHIM.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The principles behind CHIM can be taken further to mean that the Godhead and it's dreams are a metaphor for the computer running the game and the game itself. In-universe the metaphor of the godhead and being awake within the dream is needed to prevent characters who realize this from zero-summing out of existence at the resulting paradox. It can be inferred that a character who achieves CHIM essentially gains access to the console and the Construction Set. Talos used the Construction Set to retcon Cyrodiil from a jungle land into a generic European fantasy land (Talos has a terrible imagination). Vivec gave himself levitation abilities by using the console to erase the texture file for his chair (no seriously). Whether or not the player achieves CHIM varies. Generally when a player becomes fully immersed in the game, they do not have CHIM. However, a player who gets fed up of getting bugged by cliff racers every five seconds and installs a mod that removes them from the game is using CHIM. They are remembering that the world they are in is a game and altering it as they see fit. Exploits, mods, console commands, etc can all be explained in-universe as the player character achieving CHIM and using it to reshape reality or bend its rules...or all of that could be stupid speculation.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T04:39:50-07:00","id":292884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/292267-the-elder-scrolls-appreciation-discussion-thread?p=292461#post292461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who does not hate Thalmor? Even Alduin is more 'sympathetic' because even if he destroys the world new kalpa will happen (though he gone gonzo and it''s implied he wants to rule over the world). Thalmor wants to stop the cycle. But still, Molag Bal is worse, though there is style to his monstrosity.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the lore former writers and an ascended fan that on one side says he wants TES to be open content and on the other hand is so pushy about his vison being canon (and his rabid fanboys don't help either) basically wanks to the thalmor. In one of his pieces of lore about how everything ends, the Thalmor win, all humans are exterminated and the khajit go to live on the moon (good for the khajit, I guess). He also insist a lot in that that future is completly unavoidable.<br /> <br /> Molag Bal is a mixed one for me. On one hand, vampires! Yay! On the other hand &quot;King of Rape&quot;, ewwww, no.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T04:51:40-07:00","id":292888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He also insist a lot in that that future is completly unavoidable. </div> </div> </div>Kalpa will end smoothly provided Alduin comes back in more sane way. Things will just reset to the moment of creation and all souls of mortal races will materialize again as mortal races, Thalmor is just butthurt about whole cycle stuff (don't confuse them with Altmer, Mer are generally unhappy about it, but are resigned, and Thalmor has its opposition in Summerset Isles. Dunmer on another hand sees that cycle in positive way as a sort of test).<br /> <br /> I say we just need another divine made killer cyborg from future sent to ensure the survival of humanity, in other words another Pelinal &quot;Star Made Knight&quot; Whitestrake.<br /> <br /> Or possibly Last Dragonborn will get shit done post Skyrim and help whip Imperium into shape just like Talos and Reman &quot;The Worldly God&quot; Cyrodiil. Maybe convincing Akaviri to join in on the fun because of his/her Dragonborn status.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In one of his pieces of lore about how everything ends, the Thalmor win, all humans are exterminated and the khajit go to live on the moon (good for the khajit, I guess). He also insist a lot in that that future is completly unavoidable. </div> </div> </div>He reminds me of that Eldar supremacist who claims that humanity should have been exterminated in Horus Heresy because that's solution to stop Chaos. Didn't Eldar basically orgied one of Ruinous Powers into existence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 10-26-2014, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T04:54:25-07:00","id":292891,"title":"","content":"Big fan of the games as well. I think I'm the only person I know who loves Redguards. Always have. Never got a chance to play the Elder Scroll Adventure spin-off game starring one because the computer I had at the time was pretty crappy, and I remember the misery I felt trying to play Daggerfall. Crash to desktop. Sigh.<br /> <br /> Oh well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T04:58:59-07:00","id":292892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think I'm the only person I know who loves Redguards. </div> </div> </div>You are wrong. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T05:43:29-07:00","id":292903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Didn't Eldar basically orgied one of Ruinous Powers into existence? </div> </div> </div>Shlanesh, yes. They got pretty owned by it, getting most of their souls devoured on the brink of its birth, wich also created the Eye of Terror. It is the reason every Eldar now haves a soul stone on at all times, so when they die it gets trapped there instead of going into the maw of the Chaos god(dess) they spawned, wich is the default for eldar souls since then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T05:46:37-07:00","id":292908,"title":"","content":"That was rhetorical question, since I'm into Fantasy Battle/40K as much as TES.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T07:18:55-07:00","id":292955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/292267-the-elder-scrolls-appreciation-discussion-thread?p=292853#post292853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A legit explanation is that Talos did it through CHIM.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The principles behind CHIM can be taken further to mean that the Godhead and it's dreams are a metaphor for the computer running the game and the game itself. In-universe the metaphor of the godhead and being awake within the dream is needed to prevent characters who realize this from zero-summing out of existence at the resulting paradox. It can be inferred that a character who achieves CHIM essentially gains access to the console and the Construction Set. Talos used the Construction Set to retcon Cyrodiil from a jungle land into a generic European fantasy land (Talos has a terrible imagination). Vivec gave himself levitation abilities by using the console to erase the texture file for his chair (no seriously). Whether or not the player achieves CHIM varies. Generally when a player becomes fully immersed in the game, they do not have CHIM. However, a player who gets fed up of getting bugged by cliff racers every five seconds and installs a mod that removes them from the game is using CHIM. They are remembering that the world they are in is a game and altering it as they see fit. Exploits, mods, console commands, etc can all be explained in-universe as the player character achieving CHIM and using it to reshape reality or bend its rules...or all of that could be stupid speculation.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I'm quite aware of the explanation for the retcon. I just think it should never have been retconned - as it would have been seven-thousand times more interesting than the Cyrodiil we saw. Someone needs to CHIM it back to the awesomeness it deserves.<br /> <br /> God damnit, Tiber. If I weren't too busy mantling you, I'd punch you.<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Big fan of the games as well. I think I'm the only person I know who loves Redguards. Always have. Never got a chance to play the Elder Scroll Adventure spin-off game starring one because the computer I had at the time was pretty crappy, and I remember the misery I felt trying to play Daggerfall. Crash to desktop. Sigh.<br /> <br /> Oh well.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> </span><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I really like Redguards, actually. They are my favourite Human race by a very wide margin. Of course, my utter love rests with the Dunmer and Beast-Races.</span><br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T07:24:14-07:00","id":292958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> God damnit, Tiber. If I weren't too busy mantling you, I'd punch you. </div> </div> </div>That's why Vivec is more awesome. He has crazy ideas and had Sheogorath as his lawyer once. Talos is a simple man of simple tastes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T09:33:57-07:00","id":292996,"title":"","content":"I finally got around to Skyrim a few months ago; it is my introduction to The Elder Scrolls. I love it, and I have plans to download some mods for it for a second playthrough. (My first character's story just feels complete. Like I reached the perfect stopping point for him.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T09:36:33-07:00","id":292997,"title":"","content":"DLCs or without?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T14:59:51-07:00","id":293231,"title":"","content":"TES features probably the most realized fantasty universe ever to be featured in a video game, thanks in no small part to the more Esoteric aspects of it's lore that can only be found outside the games","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Do the dead dare walk the Earth before my eyes? Will the undead raise an army, fall in, and advance? Will those who would abandon God and embrace the heretical order DARE to presume to meet my gaze!? Iscariot will not allow it. <b>I</b> will not allow it.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3889-ninjasantaclause","name":"Ninjasantaclause","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T18:07:30-07:00","id":293330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/292267-the-elder-scrolls-appreciation-discussion-thread?p=292996#post292996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I finally got around to Skyrim a few months ago; it is my introduction to The Elder Scrolls. I love it, and I have plans to download some mods for it for a second playthrough. (My first character's story just feels complete. Like I reached the perfect stopping point for him.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat, what sort of character did you play?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T03:38:57-07:00","id":293616,"title":"","content":"I think of marathoning Morrowind/Oblivion/Skyrim once again. In that order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T06:48:11-07:00","id":293699,"title":"","content":"I got my introduction to The Elder Scrolls back with a game I never new was an Elder Scrolls game until 3 days ago: Battlespire. I fucking hated it. 1st person view for swinging swords and axes was just not fun in the slightest. Because of that game, I have not played any other TES game since...Until Skyrim. I have put 200ish hours into Skyrim, and not one minute of it played swinging a sword or other melee weapon. 3rd person view was horribly implemented, and if you used it for archery/spellcasting you'd miss because the reticle was not on target. Except for Vampire Lord mode, I played the whole thing slinging spells or shooting bows from 1st person. I figured: I hate 1st person RPG idea, but I can treat it pretty much like a shooter. And so I've played it for 140 hours on one character, and started a new one thats 60ish hours in at this point.<br /> Very little modding, and no mods that change game-play either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/771-starmage21","name":"Starmage21","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T06:55:40-07:00","id":293701,"title":"","content":"1st person RPGs provide better immersion since IRL I don't see my body from 3rd person perspective. Unless I'm more drugged than Charlie Sheen, maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T07:48:40-07:00","id":293720,"title":"","content":"I've played Morrowind Oblivion, and Skyrim with all expansions. I keep debating with myself if I want to give Arena or Daggerfall a shot, and never quite get around to it.<br /> <br /> I like the series a lot, mostly because it fills an urge I have to wander around aimlessly, killing, looting, and breaking down doors indiscriminately. I am a very violent and directionless explorer, which can be a lot of fun for a few dozen hours.<br /> <br /> Anyone here play the Nehrim mod? I'm going through it now, and so far it has been pretty interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T11:04:04-07:00","id":293914,"title":"","content":"First game of the series I remember is Dagerfall. I didn't even played it, I just saw it on the house of a friend while his older brother played it. I remeber the first person view and how he masacred a whole village as a were-boar. I want to play Dagerfall (it is even free online) but I don't know if I would manage to install it as i need an MS-DOS virtual machine and I'm oh so bad with computers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T11:16:42-07:00","id":293935,"title":"","content":"Mind you, you should still expect bugs in largest cRPG in history area wise, but here, this may help with running it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.uesp.net/wiki/General:Playing_DOS_Installments_under_DOSBox\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://images.uesp.net/a/ac/Featured_star.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.uesp.net/wiki/General:Playing_DOS_Installments_under_DOSBox\" target=\"_blank\"> General:Playing DOS Installments under DOSBox - UESP Wiki - The Unofficial Elder Scrolls Pages </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.uesp.net/wiki/General:Playing_DOS_Installments_under_DOSBox\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.uesp.net/wiki/General:Playing_DOS_Installments_under_DOSBox </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Earlier installments in the Elder Scrolls series&mdash;Arena, Daggerfall, Battlespire, and Redguard&mdash;were developed for DOS and consequently do not run under modern Windows (nor non-Windows systems, for that matter). This page deals specifically with running these games in DOSBox, and is applicable to all of them. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.uesp.net/wiki/Daggerfall:Running_under_Windows\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.uesp.net/w/skins/UespMonoBook/search-icon.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.uesp.net/wiki/Daggerfall:Running_under_Windows\" target=\"_blank\"> Daggerfall:Running under Windows - UESP Wiki - The Unofficial Elder Scrolls Pages </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.uesp.net/wiki/Daggerfall:Running_under_Windows\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.uesp.net/wiki/Daggerfall:Running_under_Windows </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> There is a serious memory issue when running Daggerfall under a modern Windows-OS such as Windows-XP. This issue causes the quest object to be invisible, hence it will be nearly impossible to find or kill a quest object, since it cannot be seen. Once the quest is active, switching to DosBox or similar applications doesn't solve this problem, since the quest data is already stored in your savegame, you have to start the quest from the scratch. Always keep that in mind because, if you embark on the main quest or a questline, you will have serious troubles. In addition to the problems with the quest object strafe, backward moves, climbing, swimming and jumping are almost impossible to perform. Considering all these facts, it is highly advised to use DOSBox when running Daggerfall under a modern Windows-OS. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T12:49:54-07:00","id":294053,"title":"","content":"For the curious, my first character was a Redguard sword-and-shield heavy warrior (though in retrospect, I probably should have gone with light armor considering how much sneaking I did). He grew up in Hammerfell, raised on stories of how his people drove off the elves after being abandoned by the weak and callous Empire. Hearing of the Stormcloak Rebellion, he joined up with a crew of piratical adventurers who were on their way to join the fight against the Empire (and, by extension, the Aldmeri Dominion). They were shipwrecked, though, and my character was the only survivor. He followed one faint lead after another and was finally able to join up with Ulfric--right in time to be captured with him.<br /> <br /> As for the stopping point, well, all the major plots are wrapped up: the world is saved, Skyrim is an independent nation, and my character has returned to Jorrvaskr to take his place as Harbinger of the Companions. It felt like a good place to fade to black and roll credits. For my next character, I'm going to take the Empire's side in the war, and I'm leaning toward a Dark Elf &quot;spellsword&quot; type.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ninjasantaclause</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/292267-the-elder-scrolls-appreciation-discussion-thread?p=293231#post293231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TES features probably the most realized fantasy universe ever to be featured in a video game, thanks in no small part to the more Esoteric aspects of it's lore that can only be found outside the games</div> </div> </div> </div>I really liked the verisimilitude of the Civil War plot. Neither side feels like the official &quot;hero&quot; faction (except at the very beginning) and if you replaced the names of the races, places and people with names from Eastern Europe it would read like the plot of a plausible spy novel. Conflicting values systems, difficult political choices, ethnic tensions both long-standing and recent--it's all there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T14:39:46-07:00","id":294158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/292267-the-elder-scrolls-appreciation-discussion-thread?p=292891#post292891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Big fan of the games as well. I think I'm the only person I know who loves Redguards. Always have. Never got a chance to play the Elder Scroll Adventure spin-off game starring one because the computer I had at the time was pretty crappy, and I remember the misery I felt trying to play Daggerfall. Crash to desktop. Sigh.<br /> <br /> Oh well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Redguards are my favorite group, and <i>Redguard</i> is a criminally underappreciated game. It's an early <i>Tomb Raider</i> game crossed with an Errol Flynn movie... I can't <i>not</i> love it.<br /> <br /> I still have a copy on CD somewhere. I should see if I can get it running with a modern gamepad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T14:54:05-07:00","id":294171,"title":"","content":"I play skyrim still sometimes. I play it heavily modded though. Usually with touhou skins on some characters and I've got all the guards for each city as a different vocaloid (Gumi [yes I know she's technically not a vocaloid] guards Markath, Miku guards Riften)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T15:52:39-07:00","id":294228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/292267-the-elder-scrolls-appreciation-discussion-thread?p=294158#post294158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Redguards are my favorite group, and <i>Redguard</i> is a criminally underappreciated game. It's an early <i>Tomb Raider</i> game crossed with an Errol Flynn movie... I can't <i>not</i> love it.<br /> <br /> I still have a copy on CD somewhere. I should see if I can get it running with a modern gamepad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the Redguard Elder Scrolls game difficult to get running on a modern PC? I ask this as someone who's extremely inept when it comes to