ber","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T05:04:28-08:00","id":308049,"title":"","content":"I like manly men <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My last and better character in Skyrim is a somewhat Reachmen-like Breton Necromancer with a blind eye and a badass moustache.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T05:09:17-08:00","id":308051,"title":"","content":"If anyone haven't guessed yet from set, I like blondes, so Nord girls are option in every installment that I choose at least once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T07:21:21-08:00","id":308183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/292267-the-elder-scrolls-appreciation-discussion-thread?p=308033#post308033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Question, what kind of gender you usually choose for characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually prefer to play characters of my own gender, but I have quite a few females for the sake of variety and diversity. My Bosmer warrior in Skyrim and my Dunmer Mage in Oblivion, for example.<br /> I've always role-played my Nerevarine as a man in a woman's body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T11:57:09-08:00","id":308417,"title":"","content":"If anyone wants to try Daggerfall, there's a third party wizard that installs it and bundle of patches in a rather user friendly way. It also adds some quests like an alternative way dealing with Cyndassa's werewolf and you didn't have to type command lines to start it up. That's what I used to use and you should be able to download it from the page below.<br /> Well, it turns out there <i>isn't</i> in link below, but you'll find it if you search &quot;Daggerfall installer&quot;. I saw it on that French TES fan site.<br /> <br /> I play men by default because I am one and, well, just look at us. I tend not to be very creative with them though. When I play women, they're usually rip offs of other female characters. I did that in Daggerfall in particular, nearly always playing a Breton city girl. They'd be &quot;inspired by&quot; Elle from <i>Heroes</i>, Molly Wright from <i>New Wave Requiem</i> (my introduction to VtR), Frances Black. My current Skyrim character's a restoration based Imperial spellsword and a cross between a standard LG Paladin, Joan of Arc and Lucretia from <i>Spartacus</i> with a massive messiah complex. While other characters I've played have been quite humble being Dragonborn, she thinks of herself as the last daughter of Akatosh who must slay her ancient brothers who abused their power, and the new Talos who'll bring the Empire back together forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 11-10-2014, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T09:02:37-08:00","id":309207,"title":"","content":"I'm worried that in the long run I will have it more difficult. I use kosher tricks to gain levels quickly without much combat and aside from Archery my other combats skills are woefully weak. 7th level, did not leave the village yet. Will now venture to the local mine for training on Bandits there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T09:31:04-08:00","id":309230,"title":"","content":"Wich Skills are your character strong on, Kat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T09:41:39-08:00","id":309236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wich Skills are your character strong on, Kat? </div> </div> </div>Archery so far, but due to training extensively thanks to Faendal. Pickpocketing, but only I want to put perks for extra capacity. Alchemy because I farmed that for experience, not sure yet if I will put perks there. I plan to go for Archery/Light Armor/Sneak as primary, Two Handed in a pinch when sneaking fails, Smithing/Enchanting to pimp Dragonbone Scale armors. Vampirism gives perks to Illusion, so maybe I will go for that with spare perks, and maybe Alchemy. I won't use Vampire Lord form, too impractical 